      "text": "Platform notes",
      "originalText": "Platform notes",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "text-102",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1037,
      "width": 1786.4,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 807738,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 10682358,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reference: briareus-windows. Other clients match this structure, differing only as noted here.\nThe settings sidebar is the app's own, not the preset: ← Back to sessions, This computer (🎙 Meeting assistant), Mail, Projects, Providers, Database pool, SSH servers, Forge accounts and MCP servers, each with ＋ New where allowed,\nthen a footer with 'Settings' and ⎋ Sign out. It has no Devices and clients row.\nProject dots: filled (idle) means active, a grey dot means switched off. A 'db' chip marks a project with the database pool on. ↑ and ↓ show on the open or hovered row, and right-clicking a row gives Move up / Move down.\nThe header shows the label in large type with the repo under it. Save (Ctrl+S) has an icon and the label 'Save'; ⧉ clone and 🗑 delete are icon-only buttons. A new project shows only Save, under the subtitle 'A project is a\nrepository a session can be started against.'\nA tab with unsaved changes gets a ' •' after its title. The open tab stays open when you switch to another project. A field the server's project rows do not carry is hidden.\nWith the Active box cleared, a note appears: 'Inactive: no session can be started on it and it is left out of the project lists; …'.\nWithout an Admin token, the Projects section shows a sentence explaining the token is needed instead of the rows.\nRegion names (sidebar, canvas, raise, sunken) are the theme.* roles; widths and margins are layout.* in tokens/. Greys only, on purpose.",
      "originalText": "Reference: briareus-windows. Other clients match this structure, differing only as noted here.\nThe settings sidebar is the app's own, not the preset: ← Back to sessions, This computer (🎙 Meeting assistant), Mail, Projects, Providers, Database pool, SSH servers, Forge accounts and MCP servers, each with ＋ New where allowed,\nthen a footer with 'Settings' and ⎋ Sign out. It has no Devices and clients row.\nProject dots: filled (idle) means active, a grey dot means switched off. A 'db' chip marks a project with the database pool on. ↑ and ↓ show on the open or hovered row, and right-clicking a row gives Move up / Move down.\nThe header shows the label in large type with the repo under it. Save (Ctrl+S) has an icon and the label 'Save'; ⧉ clone and 🗑 delete are icon-only buttons. A new project shows only Save, under the subtitle 'A project is a\nrepository a session can be started against.'\nA tab with unsaved changes gets a ' •' after its title. The open tab stays open when you switch to another project. A field the server's project rows do not carry is hidden.\nWith the Active box cleared, a note appears: 'Inactive: no session can be started on it and it is left out of the project lists; …'.\nWithout an Admin token, the Projects section shows a sentence explaining the token is needed instead of the rows.\nRegion names (sidebar, canvas, raise, sunken) are the theme.* roles; widths and margins are layout.* in tokens/. Greys only, on purpose.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    }
  ],
